# rvoip workspace ignore rules.
#
# Keep this file scoped to things generated by a build, produced by tooling, or
# controlled by an individual developer. Debugging leftovers that only appear
# during manual investigation belong in .git/info/exclude, not here.
#
# The `!` negations below are load-bearing — CI and the release attestations
# read the paths they preserve. Do not drop one without checking what uses it.

## Build output
# No leading slash: workspace members and fuzz targets carry their own target/
# dir, and CARGO_TARGET_DIR may point somewhere nested.
target/
debug/
release/
# `release/` above is a bare pattern for nested cargo profile dirs, so it also
# matches scripts/release/ — the gate catalog and runners that
# .github/workflows/release-qualify.yml invokes. Keep them tracked.
!scripts/release/
*.rs.bk
*.pdb
*.rlib
*.rmeta
/build
/build-rust-analyzer/
/dist/
/obj/
/vendor

## Lockfiles
# Ignored everywhere except the workspace root and examples/, whose lockfiles
# are committed on purpose. CI exercises this exact scoping.
Cargo.lock
!/Cargo.lock
!/examples/Cargo.lock
Cargo.toml.backup
Cargo.backup

## Secrets and certificates (never commit these!)
certs/
*.crt
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

## crates.io release tooling — run locally, never tracked in the repo.
publish_order.sh
scripts/check-publish-readiness.sh
scripts/publish-beta.sh
scripts/publish-dry-run.sh
scripts/prune-obsolete.sh
/scripts/sync_beta_train_versions.sh
/scripts/publish_beta_train_0.2.2.sh

## Generated test and release evidence
test_vectors/
*.db
# rvoip-sip beta report bundle — regenerated, not source.
crates/sip/rvoip-sip/beta-report/
# Perf scenario results (sipp).
crates/sip/rvoip-sip/tests/perf/sipp_scenarios/results/*
# codec-core G.711 roundtrip outputs. The `sweep-r.*` files (a, a-a,
# rea, reu, u, u-u) are codec round-trip results regenerated by
# `cargo test -p rvoip-codec-core`; only `sweep.src` is the input.
crates/media/codec-core/src/codecs/g711/tests/test_data/sweep-r.*
crates/media/codec-core/src/codecs/g711/tests/test_data/*_roundtrip_*.wav
# Audio test outputs (.wav covers most regenerated audio fixtures).
*.wav
# ...but the G.711 roundtrip *input* is a tracked fixture, not an output.
# Untracking it makes wav_roundtrip_test download over the network and panic
# when offline. The `*_roundtrip_*.wav` rule above already covers the outputs.
!crates/media/codec-core/src/codecs/g711/tests/test_data/OSR_us_000_0010_8k.wav
# Scratch analysis output.
outputs/

## Logs
*.log
# Immutable v0.3.2 release-exception evidence referenced by its attestation.
!crates/sip/rvoip-sip/docs/releases/beta/20260729T010954Z/exception-r1/source/performance-gate-metrics.log

## Profiling artifacts (see crates/sip/rvoip-sip/docs/PROFILING.md)
# `target/criterion/` and `target/flamegraphs/` are already covered by
# `target/` above; listed explicitly so the convention is discoverable
# from `.gitignore` alone.
target/criterion/
target/flamegraphs/
dhat-heap.json
dhat-heap-*.json
# samply / cargo-flamegraph output. Scoped to the generated filenames rather
# than a blanket `*.svg`, so committed diagrams and the brand assets at the
# workspace root stay visible.
flamegraph.svg
flamegraph-*.svg
perf.data
perf.data.old
*.profraw
*.profdata
osx_trace.sh
*.trace

## Node
node_modules
package-lock.json
package.json
!tests/browser-smoke/package-lock.json
!tests/browser-smoke/package.json

## Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

## OS
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db

## Editors
.idea
.vscode
.zed/
.helix/
.vim/
.settings/
.vs/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
Session.vim
.cproject
.project
.favorites.json
.dir-locals.el
# Editor / sed backups. `*-e` is what macOS `sed -i '' ...` produces
# when you forget `-i .bak` — these crept into the tree historically.
*.bak
*.orig
*-e

## Temporary files
*~
\#*
\#*\#
.#*

## Tags
tags
tags.*
TAGS
TAGS.*

## Tooling and local environment
.valgrindrc
.cargo
/.envrc
/.direnv/
/flake.nix
flake.lock
/default.nix
/bootstrap.toml
/config.toml
/Makefile
config.mk
config.stamp

## CCD session state — never publish.
.claude/

## PBX interop labs
# Local env: machine-specific addresses and credentials. The committed
# *.env.example files are the templates; a real env/<provider>.env is sourced
# after the lab-generated ~/Developer/<provider>/*-local.env and therefore
# OVERRIDES it, so committing one silently redirects the release runners at a
# developer's own lab addresses.
crates/sip/rvoip-sip/examples/pbx/env/*.env
!crates/sip/rvoip-sip/examples/pbx/env/*.env.example
# Run artifacts: logs, WAVs, pcaps, matrix.tsv and per-role metadata, all
# regenerated by every ./run.sh. Nothing reads the committed copy — the
# release gates write their evidence to PBX_OUT_ROOT (the artifact dir)
# instead — and the files embed absolute paths from whichever machine
# produced them, so committing them adds churn and leaks local layout.
crates/sip/rvoip-sip/examples/pbx/output/
# Proxy lab configs rendered by up.sh from the .in templates, with the run's
# public host, ports and a freshly generated TLS key beside them. Regenerated
# every bring-up and machine-specific; the templates are what is tracked.
infra/release-runners/pbx/*/.rendered/
